# MoOS Mo AI brain — the fast, instruct (non-thinking) chat model.
#
# WHY: the desktop chat was migrated live to a Qwen3-VL *thinking* build whose
# renderer forces long chains of thought — a trivial "reply with three words"
# cost 3700+ reasoning tokens and ~97 s, and a baked system prompt forced Arabic
# even for English input. Measured. A non-thinking instruct model answers the
# same query in <0.5 s, in the language it was asked in, and follows the app's
# own bilingual system prompt.
#
# Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct Q4 is GPU-resident on the 8 GB RTX 2080 SUPER. num_ctx is
# 24576, NOT 8192: the desktop chat sends a short prompt, but the SAME model also
# serves the Telegram agent (OpenClaw), whose system+tools prompt ALONE is ~11.5k
# tokens. At 8192 it overflowed before a single user word; at 16384 the first
# reply worked but a few multi-turn messages (base ~11.5k + history) overran the
# ~14.3k budget and the bot errored again. 24576 leaves ~11k tokens for the actual
# conversation on top of the base prompt; measured 4.7 GB model / 6.8 GB total on
# this card (the model natively supports 32768). OpenClaw's contextTokens must
# match — moos-ensure-brain reconciles openclaw.json to this value.
# No baked SYSTEM: main.qml sends the real Mo AI system prompt + live machine
# context, so the model must not carry its own.
FROM qwen2.5:7b-instruct
SYSTEM ""
PARAMETER num_ctx 24576
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
